      "writtenOn": "2022-11-09T10:10:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What if the list of interfaces change during discovery ? MulticastNetworkInterfaceProvider doesn\u0027t seem very helpful for that.\n\nIt also doesn\u0027t help linking interfaces with their Network object, which would be very helpful in aosp/2239480: MulticastNetworkInterfaceProvider is updated based on network callbacks.\n\nI think you could have a replacement for MulticastNetworkInterfaceProvider which:\n\n - Registers a network callback\n - Also registers a TetheringEventCallback to know about tethered interfaces\n - Associates a Network with each MdnsSocketClient on creation, since they are created from Connectivity or Tethering (LOCAL_NET_ID) callbacks; then you can use it to find the right network for aosp/2239480\n - Handles starting discovery on new interfaces if they come up while discovery is in progress for all interfaces",
      "revId": "f06fed0913d5acc696be233cbec7703aab765c6e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
